From c3ccdd218b2cdb3e27dc0990509e5e2de3ee6cf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:50:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(xtask): a failed test build stops the quick gate and
 names the metadata error

A failed `<crate> build (--no-run)` step now stops a one-at-a-time plan, as
`debug build (--no-run)` did. The summary lists the later steps as
`SKIP ... not run (build failed: <step>)` and the gate exits red.

A failed step whose log has a rustc metadata error (E0786 "found invalid
metadata files", E0460 "found possibly newer version") prints a BUILD FAULT
block: the crate of the error, and the two commands to try
(CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4, cargo clean -p <package of the step>). No automatic
retry or clean. The cause of #3601 stays open.

Refs #3601

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
